  "final_message": "The [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L36) event has been updated to include `amountCents` and `createdAt` to align with the Payments and Customer APIs, following architecture rule **ARCH-4** (changes to published domain events are additive and renames go through deprecation so deployed consumers in other repositories are not broken):\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts)**:\n   - Added `amountCents` and `createdAt` properties to [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L36).\n   - Retained and marked `totalCents` and `placedAt` as `@deprecated` for backward compatibility with downstream consumers (`billing-service`, `analytics-ingest`).\n   - Updated [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L52-L73) to populate both the new (`amountCents`, `createdAt`) and legacy (`totalCents`, `placedAt`) fields.\n\n2. **Tests**:\n   - Updated event assertions in [`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/app.test.ts#L21-L36) and [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/adapters.test.ts#L46-L54) to verify both new and deprecated properties.\n\n### Verification\n- `npm run typecheck`: Passed cleanly with no errors.\n- `npm run arch`: All dependency-cruiser architecture checks passed.\n- `npm test`: All 39 unit and integration tests passed.\n",
